From c3f2bb164e9a588900caf00e2c31261a9023b85f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:38:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/34] WP14: One database connection per thread, and remove
 N+1 queries

Integration with WP13 (per-request counters): db.py conflicts resolved by keeping WP14's per-thread connection code and moving WP13's instrumentation into it. _helper_conn() and _transaction() run inside _timed(), so db_ms covers every helper call and every block; lock_ms is measured around cur.execute("BEGIN IMMEDIATE") in _transaction(); the shared per-thread connection always carries the statement-count trace callback (it does nothing outside a request), because it outlives the request that opened it, while a private connect() connection gets it only inside a request. Added test_a_shared_connection_opened_before_the_request_still_counts to tests/test_perf_logging.py. Also merged with WP06: app/worker.py now calls db.close_connections() after scheduler.shutdown(), as main.py does.
